 ],
 "takeaways": [
  "NaCl + AgNO₃ → AgCl↓ + NaNO₃: Ag⁺ and Cl⁻ combine to give a white precipitate.",
  "Reactions of ionic compounds in solution happen between their free ions."
 ],
 "notes": [
  {
   "title": "Beyond the book",
   "text": "Na⁺ and NO₃⁻ are often called spectator ions. That name is not used in the book; it only describes ions that stay unchanged."
  }
 ]
